  "shortDescription": "Hitchhiking for a cause. To build an Earthship Community center in Malawi Africa by raising money and awareness across the country.",
  "projectStory": "Project story\nCreator\nErica Izor\nmore infocontact\nCategory\nEnvironment\nTags\nother\nBacking information\nCrowdfunding risks\nlearn more\nThis October Earthship Biotecture is teaming up with The Kapita Development Committee (KDC) and Empower Malawi Limited- a local not for profit organization, to build a sustainable development epicenter for 38 villages and over 5,000 people in Malawi.\n \nNot only will the project include a community bank, a mini library, a dispensary, offices and a food bank, but the peoples of Malawi will be left with an invaluable skill, the ability to build and maintain sustainable autonomous structures that can be used as businesses or homes in order to put the power of their lives, back in their own hands.\nTo learn more about the project and see their official video:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-dKEuFCOhPA\nSo- in order to raise awareness and money, my goal is around a dollar a mile.. By hitchhiking from my hometown in Vermont to The Greater World Earthship Community outside Taos New Mexico. With a tire. \nWhy? Its necessary to not only help people in ways that truly benefit their community, but where the real growth continues to happen long after the initial help has gone. To give people the knowledge tools and resources to take their lives back and have their well being subject to no other power besides themselves.\nPlease Donate. Or Volunteer. A Greater World is Waiting.",
